    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0758" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Tri-Motors Safety Airways/63:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-08T09:00:00+01:00">July 8, 1929—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 9—7:44 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>324. Have vigorously pressed subject of Department’s telegram No. 128, April 30,
                    2 p.m.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d478-f1"/> French Government now desires to know
                    precise purpose flight, whether scientific, tour, or preparation establishment
                    air line via French possessions. In the latter case delay and possible
                    difficulties anticipated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
